    "axis": "clarity",
    "evidence": "The headline clearly states that cryptographic validity and semantic validity are separate, and the intent→cart→payment example makes the mismatch visible across viewports. However, “release-custodied scorer,” “public-seed synthetic signer keys,” “results artifact,” “semantic invariant,” and “NOT_PRESENT” require domain interpretation. The apparent next action, “Inspect semantic mismatch,” is ambiguous because the mismatch is already displayed, while the mobile header hides Mandate behind “More.”",
    "fix": "Use plain-language labels, rename the CTA to describe its actual effect (for example, “Show why this payment violates the intent”), and add one explicit verdict beside the checks: “Signatures valid; transaction unauthorized.”",
